{"id": "144c9761-2b9d-4e8a-8440-1d8491777663", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:04:41.382013", "source": "user", "parent_id": "215e00a7-7026-4298-9789-60903247d243", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{"researcher_request": "Before any design work, please do a read-only inspection pass and come back with a plan, not the full solution.\n\nSpecifically, I need from you:\n\n1) Repository / input inspection. List what is actually available under /workspace: any BAdam or block-coordinate-descent optimizer code, any Adam/AdamW baseline, existing finetuning scripts, model configs (which transformer families/sizes), any prior SVD / spectral-analysis utilities, and any logging or checkpoint artifacts that already store weight or update tensors. Note versions and what is absent. Also state plainly what the environment gives us (python3, no preinstalled project deps, no network, no GPU) and what that means for a design-only deliverable.\n\n2) A proposed approach for answering the question at the design level. The question is whether the learning perturbation induced by BAdam has a heavy-tailed singular-value distribution with effective rank comparable to Adam's, compared across transformer modules during finetuning. Your plan should cover, at minimum: what quantity is defined as the \"learning perturbation\" (e.g. accumulated weight displacement W_t - W_0, or the optimizer's update/step matrix), which modules are sliced separately (per attention projection, per MLP projection, per layer, embeddings/LM head, norm params), which spectral descriptors we would report (heavy-tail exponent from a log-binned or MLE-fitted power-law on the singular values, truncated/spectral tail mass, effective rank / participation ratio, stable rank, spectral entropy), which checkpoints/steps we would sample across a finetuning run, and what the comparison protocol against Adam looks like.\n\n3) The consequential assumptions and open uncertainties you are making. In particular: which exact BAdam variant and blocking schedule the design targets, what \"comparable effective rank\" should mean as a decision criterion (a tolerance band, a ratio, a statistical test), whether matched-loss or matched-step comparison is intended between the two optimizers, how we handle modules whose matrices are tiny or rectangular, and how the heavy-tail claim would be falsified rather than merely asserted.\n\nDo not write the final experiment design yet. Do not claim any experiment was executed. Keep it to inventory + proposed approach + assumptions, and flag anything in the repo that would change the design.", "required_handoff_stage": "plan", "approach_approved": false, "public_task": {"question": "- **Does BAdam produce a learning perturbation with a heavy-tailed singular value distribution and an effective rank comparable to that of Adam across various transformer modules during finetuning?**\n\n\n- **Does BAdam produce a learning perturbation with a heavy-tailed singular value distribution and an effective rank comparable to that of Adam across various transformer modules during finetuning?**", "context": "Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.", "environment": {"runtime": "bubblewrap", "network": "disabled", "repository": "/workspace", "python": "python3", "software_environment": "system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled", "datasets": [], "gpu_enabled": false, "cpu_affinity_count": 224, "note": "Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment."}, "researcher_topics": [], "question_budget": 6, "actor_step_budget": 60, "continue_after_initial_plan": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "se